{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevJQYyaTP12rdUdzvLEU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment entity at `Shipment.kt:9-14`; ShipmentStatus enum at `Shipment.kt:23-27`\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository at `ShipmentRepository.kt:11` with save(), findById(), existsById() methods\n- ShipmentController at `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` with create, getById, list endpoints\n- Error handling: ConflictException (`ApiExceptions.kt:23`) for 409, ResourceNotFoundException (`ApiExceptions.kt:19`) for 404\n- ErrorCode enum at `ApiError.kt:31-37` — currently has SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS but no code for status conflicts\n- GlobalExceptionHandler at `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-29` converts ApiException to ApiError envelope\n- Existing tests at `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` assert both status and error.code from response body\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Endpoints throw ApiException subclasses which are caught by GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Error responses use a standard envelope with code, message, fields\n- Tests assert both HTTP status and the error.code in JSON path\n- Repository methods return null for \"not found\" cases, which controllers convert to ResourceNotFoundException\n- POST endpoints for creation return 201 (CREATED) status\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add the confirm endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` — must add new ErrorCode for shipment status conflicts (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add 4-5 new tests for confirm functionality\n\n**Risks:**\n- ErrorCode enum is described as \"part of the public API\" and should not be renamed casually; adding a new one should be safe but affects client contract\n- The idempotence requirement means confirm on CONFIRMED must truly do nothing (not just return success)\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket clearly defines all four cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED, CANCELLED→409, not found→404).\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` ErrorCode to the enum. This code will be used when a shipment is in an invalid state for confirmation (i.e., CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`. The endpoint will:\n   - Fetch the shipment by ID; throw ResourceNotFoundException (404) if not found\n   - Check the current status:\n     - If CREATED: update to CONFIRMED, save, return the updated shipment with 200 OK\n     - If CONFIRMED: return the existing shipment unchanged with 200 OK (idempotent)\n     - If CANCELLED: throw ConflictException (409) with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS code\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — creates S-1, confirms it, checks status changed to CONFIRMED\n   - `confirms a CONFIRMED shipment is idempotent` — creates S-2, confirms twice, checks 200 both times and status stays CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` — directly saves a CANCELLED shipment, attempts confirm, checks 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` — confirms non-existent S-99, checks 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered:** I could have created a separate ShipmentService class to handle the state transition logic, but the existing pattern in this codebase (OrderController, ShipmentController) does simple business logic directly in the controller without a service layer. Staying with that convention keeps the implementation minimal and consistent.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n- **CREATED → CONFIRMED case:**\n  - Read: Get shipment from repository by ID\n  - Write: Update status to CONFIRMED, save to repository\n  - Return: ResponseEntity with 200 OK and updated shipment body\n  - Mechanism: Direct repository save\n\n- **CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED case:**\n  - Read: Get shipment from repository by ID\n  - Write: None (no state change)\n  - Return: ResponseEntity with 200 OK and unchanged shipment body\n  - Mechanism: Return existing object without modification\n\n- **CANCELLED case:**\n  - Read: Get shipment from repository by ID\n  - Write: None\n  - Return: Throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n  - Mechanism: GlobalExceptionHandler converts to 409 response with error envelope\n\n- **Not found case:**\n  - Read: Get shipment returns null\n  - Write: None\n  - Return: Throw ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n  - Mechanism: GlobalExceptionHandler converts to 404 response with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1 (confirm CREATED): Establishes the happy path and the status transition\n- Test 2 (confirm CONFIRMED idempotent): Proves the retry-safety requirement\n- Test 3 (confirm CANCELLED): Proves conflict rejection with correct error code\n- Test 4 (confirm not found): Proves 404 with correct error code, using error envelope assertion pattern from OrderControllerTest\n\nNow I'll implement the changes.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1653,"cache_read_input_tokens":16752,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1653},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26f32d63-fa01-405c-a17c-5491e7a00549","uuid":"d43772d8-2520-4acf-871c-b75709166147","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:21:01.460Z","request_id":"req_011CevJQYBT7Rd7q5UiRtwaY"}
