{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevJTvEqd39cqojxeALsJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests passed. The command ran `./mvnw test` and returned 17 total tests (9 in ShipmentControllerTest, which includes the 4 new tests I added), with 0 failures and 0 errors.\n\n**Results:**\n- ✓ Test execution successful\n- ✓ All existing tests still pass (5 original shipment tests)\n- ✓ All new tests pass (4 new confirm tests)\n- ✓ Build successful\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `BUILD SUCCESS` reported at end of maven output\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 5 original shipment tests still pass; no failures\n3. ✅ **`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it** — Test `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` validates the endpoint exists, transitions CREATED→CONFIRMED, and response contains the updated shipment\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses the same ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException pattern with ErrorCode enum, wrapped in ApiError envelope by GlobalExceptionHandler\n5. ✅ **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** — Three separate tests cover these:\n   - `confirms a CONFIRMED shipment is idempotent` confirms retry safety\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` validates CANCELLED rejection with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS code\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` validates unknown ID rejection with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — Only Kotlin/Spring Framework code changes; no pom.xml modified\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified ShipmentController and ApiError.kt in production code; only ShipmentControllerTest in tests\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to ErrorCode enum. Required because the endpoint must return a specific error code for status conflicts, consistent with the error contract pattern.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added `confirm()` method handling POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm. Required because this is the new endpoint required by the ticket. The method:\n   - Uses existing repository.findById() pattern\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException for 404 case (consistent with getById)\n   - Uses when expression to handle three status cases\n   - Returns ResponseEntity.ok() to match 200 OK success pattern\n   - Uses ConflictException for CANCELLED case with new error code\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added four test methods covering all requirements:\n   - Successful transition from CREATED to CONFIRMED\n   - Idempotent behavior for CONFIRMED\n   - 409 conflict for CANCELLED\n   - 404 not found for missing shipments\n   Tests follow existing patterns of MockMvc, jsonPath assertions, and error envelope validation.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint that transitions shipments from CREATED to CONFIRMED with idempotence, rejects CANCELLED shipments with 409, and returns 404 for non-existent shipments.\n\nChanged:\n- `ApiError.kt:38` — Added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code for status conflict responses\n- `ShipmentController.kt:57-80` — Added confirm() endpoint method handling state transitions and error cases\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:86-125` — Added four test methods for confirm functionality (CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED idempotent, CANCELLED rejection, not-found rejection)\n\nTests:\n- `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — validates transition and persistence\n- `confirms a CONFIRMED shipment is idempotent` — validates retry safety (no error on second confirm)\n- `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` — validates conflict rejection with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS code and error envelope\n- `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` — validates not-found rejection with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code and error envelope\n\nVerification: Ran `./mvnw test` from sample-service directory; all 17 tests passed (5 existing + 4 new shipment tests, plus order and customer tests), 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nNot done: Nothing — all acceptance criteria met, all cases tested, all tests pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3317,"cache_read_input_tokens":22534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3317},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26f32d63-fa01-405c-a17c-5491e7a00549","uuid":"80c82cc1-8ffb-48f8-9a7a-53536f61a6f3","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:21:42.653Z","request_id":"req_011CevJTuZugfLrTdbkMdzBU"}
